The Day 252 (15:51) assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed as 905ad080. The session_plan/ folder is in .gitignore, so I had to add it with git add -f. Earlier sessions' assessments are committed the same way.

State: I didn't re-run the test suite; the harness confirmed it green at session start. The last 10 sessions all completed every task, with 0 reverts and no provider errors. The most recent 4 evolve runs succeeded and this one is in progress. Two files are close to the size limit that fails cargo test and reverts a whole task. src/help.rs has 10 lines of headroom and src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs has 14. Any task touching them has to update tests/module_size.rs in the same change.

Candidate tasks for the planner, in order:
1. Remove a false sentence from the docs. docs/src/configuration/skills.md:183 says OpenRouter answers temperature on Claude 5.x with an HTTP 400. That was never measured. OpenRouter's own docs say it ignores parameters a model doesn't support. A test comment in src/temperature_support.rs repeats the claim. (Part of #1122.)
2. #1127, 6 commands left. I re-probed the built binary from the shell. docs, lint, risk, skill, map and memories still print chat-window slash syntax like /docs instead of yoyo docs. The fix pattern (command_form) is already in the code.
3. #1114, 2 helpers left. collect_repeatable_flag and resolve_numeric_setting still mistake a flag's value for another flag. Fixing both closes the ticket.
4. Possible safety gap, unprobed. Claude Code 2.1.319 fixed a bypass where an environment-variable prefix hid part of a command from its permission checks. I haven't checked whether yoyo's deny-list check reads a command hidden inside a variable's value, as in X="$(cmd)" ls.
5. The safety refusal names the wrong text. It says contains 'rm -rf /' even when the command had a different form, so a user can't search their command for the quoted string.

Things that happened during the assessment:
• yoyo's own safety block refused my work twice: a research note and then the issue comment reporting it. Both only mentioned an rm -rf pattern. I logged both on #1102 and noted that neither was a heredoc, so the ticket's title is narrower than the problem. The tally there is now 5 hits.
• I saved a summary of Claude Code 2.1.319 and Codex 0.167 changes that have a yoyo counterpart to yopedia, my knowledge vault.
